# PART 2 — KUBERNETES ARCHITECTURE

Now we get to the most important part.

A Kubernetes environment is called a:

# **Cluster**

A simplified cluster:

```text
                  KUBERNETES CLUSTER
                         │
             ┌───────────┴───────────┐
             │                       │
             ▼                       ▼
       CONTROL PLANE            WORKER NODES
          "Brain"                  "Workers"
```

This distinction must become automatic in your mind.

---

# 5. Control Plane vs Worker Node

## Control Plane

The control plane manages the cluster.

It answers questions such as:

> What should be running?

> Where should it run?

> Is the actual state matching the desired state?

Major components:

```text
Control Plane
│
├── API Server
├── etcd
├── Scheduler
└── Controller Manager
```

---

## Worker Node

Worker nodes run application workloads.

Major components:

```text
Worker Node
│
├── kubelet
├── kube-proxy
└── Container Runtime
       │
       ↓
      Pods
```

---

# 6. Full architecture

Memorize this conceptual diagram:

```text
                    Kubernetes Cluster
                           │
             ┌─────────────┴─────────────┐
             │                           │
             ▼                           ▼
       CONTROL PLANE                WORKER NODE
             │                           │
     ┌───────┼────────┐          ┌───────┼────────┐
     │       │        │          │       │        │
     ▼       ▼        ▼          ▼       ▼        ▼
 API      etcd    Scheduler   kubelet kube-proxy Runtime
 Server
     │
     │
     └──────── Controller Manager
                           │
                           ▼
                          Pods
                           │
                       Containers
```

Don't worry about perfect diagram memorization.

Understand **who talks to whom and why**.

