# PART 11 — CRITICAL INTERVIEW DISTINCTIONS

## API Server vs etcd

| API Server                              | etcd                       |
| --------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |
| Front door/API                          | Persistent key-value store |
| Receives requests                       | Stores cluster state       |
| Authentication/authorization/validation | Stores Kubernetes data     |
| Central communication point             | Backend datastore          |

### Interview answer

> "The API Server is the central interface through which Kubernetes components and clients interact with the cluster, while etcd is the persistent distributed key-value store where Kubernetes cluster state is stored."

---

# Scheduler vs Controller

| Scheduler                      | Controller                         |
| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------- |
| Decides where a Pod should run | Reconciles desired vs actual state |
| Node selection                 | State management                   |
| Scheduling constraints         | Resource-specific controllers      |

Memory:

> **Scheduler = WHERE**

> **Controller = WHAT needs to be done to reach desired state**

---

# kubelet vs kube-proxy

| kubelet                       | kube-proxy                                 |
| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |
| Node agent                    | Service networking component               |
| Manages Pod lifecycle on node | Helps implement Service traffic routing    |
| Reports node/Pod status       | Handles networking rules/proxying behavior |

---

# kubelet vs Container Runtime

| kubelet                         | Runtime                     |
| ------------------------------- | --------------------------- |
| Manages Pod/container lifecycle | Actually runs containers    |
| Talks to API Server             | Executes container workload |
| Uses container runtime          | containerd / CRI-O          |

---

